{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115654","id":3229396689,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7AfK7R","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115654","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115654.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115654.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115654","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115654/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115654/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115654/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/bcbcb58dd3fd04a15c650fbfc006e4158c48a963","number":115654,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix hostfxr initialization treating non-zero success codes as failure","user":{"login":"thygrrr","id":8904620,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDQ2MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8904620?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr","html_url":"https://github.com/thygrrr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thygrrr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The .NET hosting API (hostfxr) defines multiple success status codes:\r\n- 0: Success\r\n- 1: Success_HostAlreadyInitialized\r\n- 2: Success_DifferentRuntimeProperties\r\n\r\nBoth `hostfxr_initialize_for_runtime_config` and\r\n`hostfxr_initialize_for_dotnet_command_line` can return these non-zero success codes (e.g. when the .NET runtime has already been initialized by a host application). The existing `rc != 0` checks incorrectly treat these as failures.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the standard .NET hosting error_codes.h (from the .NET Foundation, MIT license, https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/native/corehost/error_codes.h) and uses its `STATUS_CODE_SUCCEEDED()` macro to properly check for success (status_code >= 0), matching the documented behavior of the hosting API.\r\n\r\nThis enables libgodot with mono enabled to have a chance to be loaded from a .NET process.\r\n\r\n*(it's part of a variety of potential checks that need to succeed for this to work seamlessly, but this one is an atomic bug fix where the hostfxr spec was violated and Godot/libgodot exhibits unexpected behaviour)*\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic: